WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.944 --> 00:00:17.274
It early morning, and two workers at Shopwell Supermarket were stocking shelves.

2
00:00:19.116 --> 00:00:23.619
"We have too many canned tomatoes, Meg," one worker said, looking in boxes.

3
00:00:23.639 --> 00:00:25.740
"They won't fit on the shelf."

4
00:00:28.102 --> 00:00:30.944
"Let's stack them near the cash registers," Meg said.

5
00:00:31.948 --> 00:00:34.309
"We need to hurry—the store opens soon."

6
00:00:36.309 --> 00:00:39.570
As they carried the boxes down an aisle, Meg spotted some empty shelves.

7
00:00:39.590 --> 00:00:42.991
"We stocked those shelves earlier.

8
00:00:43.111 --> 00:00:44.352
Where did all the food go?"

9
00:00:45.292 --> 00:00:47.713
Something crunched under Daryl's foot, and he looked down.

10
00:00:48.913 --> 00:00:51.013
Crumbs and wrappers were scattered across the floor.

11
00:00:51.033 --> 00:00:54.514
"Have you been eating stuff, Daryl?"

12
00:00:54.815 --> 00:00:56.255
Meg asked, putting down her box.

13
00:00:56.275 --> 00:00:58.536
"Of course not!"

14
00:00:58.876 --> 00:00:59.616
Daryl replied.

15
00:01:00.404 --> 00:01:01.785
"Then who's been eating?"

16
00:01:02.045 --> 00:01:05.807
Snort! Startled, Daryl dropped his boxes.

17
00:01:05.827 --> 00:01:08.589
"What was that noise?"

18
00:01:09.509 --> 00:01:12.771
Meg gestured toward the end of the aisle, and they tiptoed toward the sound.

19
00:01:15.312 --> 00:01:18.454
Snort! Suddenly a large figure leaped out.

20
00:01:18.474 --> 00:01:22.376
"Ahh!" Meg and Daryl ran.

21
00:01:28.019 --> 00:01:29.060
what are you doing?"

22
00:01:29.492 --> 00:01:30.853
Miss Apricot asked with a frown.

23
00:01:32.174 --> 00:01:33.476
Jack was crawling on the floor.

24
00:01:33.496 --> 00:01:36.938
"My pencil rolled off my desk."

25
00:01:37.959 --> 00:01:38.880
Roxy reached down.

26
00:01:38.900 --> 00:01:40.301
"Here it is."

27
00:01:42.083 --> 00:01:44.665
The teacher folded her arms and gave Jack a stern look.

28
00:01:44.685 --> 00:01:51.050
"You're supposed to be reading quietly—not searching for your pencil."

29
00:01:55.434 --> 00:01:57.236
Jack sat down and spun his pencil around.

30
00:01:58.696 --> 00:01:59.836
"My book is boring.

31
00:02:00.236 --> 00:02:01.557
I wish it was time for recess."

32
00:02:01.577 --> 00:02:06.058
"I'm enjoying my book," Terrell said.

33
00:02:06.078 --> 00:02:08.399
"It's about the Silk Road."

34
00:02:09.979 --> 00:02:10.759
Mara groaned.

35
00:02:10.779 --> 00:02:13.520
"Is your book boring too?"

36
00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:14.521
Roxy asked.

37
00:02:14.541 --> 00:02:20.942
"I like my book, but I'm so hungry," Mara said.

38
00:02:20.962 --> 00:02:26.284
"I can't wait for lunch—it's Pizza Day," Terrell said.

39
00:02:27.820 --> 00:02:30.702
"Mmm, I can smell it cooking," Mara said.

40
00:02:32.142 --> 00:02:32.823
Jack sniffed.

41
00:02:32.843 --> 00:02:34.404
"Me too!"

42
00:02:35.624 --> 00:02:36.745
Miss Apricot frowned.

43
00:02:36.765 --> 00:02:40.087
"Shh!" Jack grinned sheepishly.

44
00:02:40.107 --> 00:02:43.869
"Sorry!" Roxy's watch beeped.

45
00:02:43.889 --> 00:02:47.431
"I'll be right back, Miss Apricot.

46
00:02:48.111 --> 00:02:50.732
I need to, um, use the restroom."

47
00:02:53.194 --> 00:02:55.495
Roxy ran into the hallway and opened her watch.

48
00:02:55.515 --> 00:02:57.276
"Mayor Bloom.

49
00:02:57.556 --> 00:02:58.176
What's wrong?"

50
00:02:58.196 --> 00:03:03.480
"Rocket Girl," Mayor Bloom said, "there's a food thief in Metro City."

51
00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:06.501
"A food thief?"

52
00:03:06.882 --> 00:03:07.642
Roxy repeated.

53
00:03:08.643 --> 00:03:09.543
Mayor Bloom nodded.

54
00:03:09.563 --> 00:03:12.925
"The thief is eating food without paying for it."

55
00:03:14.266 --> 00:03:15.447
"I'll check it out, Mayor.

56
00:03:15.767 --> 00:03:20.249
But I usually fight dangerous villains—not somebody who ate a meal and didn't pay."

57
00:03:20.269 --> 00:03:24.352
"The thief didn't just eat a meal," Mayor Bloom said.

58
00:03:25.084 --> 00:03:27.587
"He ate all the food at Shopwell Supermarket!"

59
00:03:27.607 --> 00:03:30.169
"Whoa!" Roxy gasped.

60
00:03:30.189 --> 00:03:35.454
"Then he ate all the food in two other food stores and several restaurants."

61
00:03:36.015 --> 00:03:37.116
Mayor Bloom shook his head.

62
00:03:37.136 --> 00:03:39.938
"He's in Metro City Bakery now."

63
00:03:41.140 --> 00:03:44.403
"The thief sounds like some sort of super eater," Roxy said.

64
00:03:44.423 --> 00:03:47.145
"Don't worry, Mayor—I'm on my way!"

65
00:03:53.196 --> 00:03:56.779
When Roxy arrived, police officers had surrounded Metro City Bakery.

66
00:03:57.980 --> 00:04:00.442
Detective Smith was watching from behind a police car.

67
00:04:01.923 --> 00:04:03.165
Roxy floated next to him.

68
00:04:03.185 --> 00:04:08.149
"Hi, Detective—I heard you have a big appetite today."

69
00:04:08.169 --> 00:04:12.873
"Very funny, Rocket Girl," Detective Smith said.

70
00:04:12.893 --> 00:04:15.675
"I didn't eat all the food."

71
00:04:15.695 --> 00:04:17.717
"Well, who did?"

72
00:04:18.077 --> 00:04:18.758
Roxy asked.

73
00:04:18.778 --> 00:04:21.380
"Do you have any information about the thief?"

74
00:04:22.528 --> 00:04:24.190
Detective Smith glanced at his notebook.

75
00:04:25.011 --> 00:04:30.456
"I interviewed two workers at Shopwell Supermarket who said the thief is a large—" Crash!

76
00:04:31.037 --> 00:04:32.559
The front of the bakery exploded.

77
00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:37.704
As the dust settled, a large figure stepped out and Roxy gasped.

78
00:04:37.724 --> 00:04:41.368
"A large pig!"
